{"page":"PRKRA","gene":"PRKRA","accession":"O75569","protein":"Interferon-inducible double-stranded RNA-dependent protein kinase activator A","length":313,"events":["Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"O75569-1","name":"1","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000325748.9"],"refseq":["NM_003690.5"],"refseqProteins":["NP_003681.1"],"maneSelect":true,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"model":{"entry":"AF-O75569-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-O75569-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":75.4,"plddt":[[0,20],[50,12],[70,18],[90,3],[70,2],[50,9],[70,3],[90,4],[70,5],[90,2],[70,8],[90,7],[70,1],[90,1],[70,6],[50,2],[0,20],[50,2],[70,1],[90,6],[70,10],[90,5],[70,2],[90,1],[70,7],[90,7],[70,4],[90,21],[70,4],[50,2],[0,16],[50,1],[70,20],[50,1],[70,1],[50,3],[70,2],[90,12],[70,3],[90,22],[70,5],[90,26],[70,4],[50,2]]}},"features":[{"type":"Region","start":1,"end":103,"description":"Sufficient for self-association and interaction with TARBP2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":18,"end":18,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Domain","start":34,"end":101,"description":"DRBM 1"},{"type":"Region","start":102,"end":195,"description":"Sufficient for self-association and interaction with TARBP2"},{"type":"Domain","start":126,"end":194,"description":"DRBM 2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":167,"end":167,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Region","start":195,"end":313,"description":"Sufficient for self-association and interaction with TARBP2"},{"type":"Domain","start":240,"end":308,"description":"DRBM 3"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":246,"end":246,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":287,"end":287,"description":"Phosphoserine"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Homodimer. Interacts with EIF2AK2/PKR through its DRBM domains. Interacts with DICER1, AGO2 and TARBP2. Also able to interact with dsRNA. Interacts with UBC9 (By similarity). Forms a complex with UBC9 and p53/TP53 (By similarity). Interacts with DUS2L (via DRBM domain). Interacts with RIGI"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with ebolavirus protein VP35; this interaction inhibits the interaction between RIGI and PRKRA. In addition, this interaction disrupts the interaction between VP35 and the viral polymerase L. So the VP35-PRKRA interaction plays a critical role in determining the outcome of ebolavirus infection (PubMed:23870315). The interaction PRKRA-VP35 also prevents PRKRA binding to DICER1 and thus allows the virus to counteract host RNA silencing (PubMed:21228243)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with human herpesvirus 8 protein MTA/ORF57; this interaction inhibits stress granule formation"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"O75569-2","name":"2","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":302,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000432031.6"],"refseq":["NM_001139517.2"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001132989.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,1],[11,22,292]],"edits":[{"start":1,"end":21,"original":"MSQSRHRAEAPPLEREDSGTF","replacement":"MQSTPFCGFC","added":10}],"missing":20,"replaced":0,"novel":9,"foldedAbsent":0,"foldedMissing":0,"features":[[0,20,0],[1,1,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-O75569-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-O75569-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":77,"plddt":[[0,10],[50,11],[70,18],[90,3],[70,2],[50,8],[70,4],[90,4],[70,5],[90,2],[70,8],[90,7],[70,1],[90,1],[70,6],[50,3],[0,20],[50,1],[70,13],[50,1],[70,4],[90,4],[70,10],[90,6],[70,6],[90,5],[70,5],[90,9],[70,4],[50,3],[0,15],[50,2],[70,22],[50,3],[70,2],[90,10],[70,5],[90,22],[70,5],[90,26],[70,5],[50,1]],"losingConfidence":0}},{"accession":"O75569-3","name":"3","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":288,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000487082.5"],"refseq":["NM_001139518.2"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001132990.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,26,288]],"edits":[{"start":1,"end":25,"original":"MSQS